# Root Dockerfile builds ONLY weclone-server (see ./Dockerfile).
#
# Whitelist strategy: exclude the whole repo, re-include the weclone-server
# subtree, then strip its local junk. This keeps the Electron application
# (root node_modules/, dist/, dist-electron/, release/, videos/, resources/,
# reference-projects/, …) out of the build context entirely — faster uploads,
# and no chance of Electron artifacts leaking into the server image.
#
# NEVER re-include anything outside weclone-server/ here.

*

!weclone-server/

# Local junk inside the server subtree (rebuilt in-image or machine-local):
weclone-server/node_modules
weclone-server/dist
weclone-server/data
weclone-server/data-test
weclone-server/.env
weclone-server/*.log
weclone-server/.server-pid.txt
weclone-server/.server-test-pid.txt
